  "body": "## What changed\n\nA 2D Pocket, 2D Adaptive, 2D Offset or 2D Contour can cut deeper below the stock top than the flute length of its tool. The operation now gives that cause first.\n\n- **Always a note, first in the notes.** It has the tool name. Text for the #3319 case:\n  `EM-0800-4FL has a flute length of 10.000 mm; this operation cuts 20.500 mm below the stock top; above the flutes, the shank or the holder goes into the cut and can rub or collide - use a tool with a flute length of at least 20.500 mm, or cut less deep`\n- **A warning `flute_short`, first in the warning list.** It comes only when the shank or holder laws convict the body on the same path (`ShankHit`, `HolderHit`, `SweepHit`). Text:\n  `the tool's flute length is 10.000 mm, but the cut goes 20.500 mm below the stock top from move N: above the flutes, the shank or the holder goes into the cut; the findings after this one name the moves where it meets material - use a tool with a longer flute, or cut less deep (this finding alone does not hold the post)`\n- **Advisory, never a block.** `blocks_post()` is false. The shank and holder findings hold the post, as before. The #3319 case stays blocked by its shank findings.\n- No verifier law, collision check or rapid check changes. The text of `RapidInStock` does not change (that is #3520).\n\nWhere:\n- The law: `crates/sim/src/verify/flute_reach.rs` (`flute_reach`, `flute_note`). It compares the lowest cutting tip with the stock top.\n- The new kind and its text: `crates/sim/src/verify/types.rs` (`Warning::FluteShort`).\n- The placement: `crates/app/src/operation/flute_law.rs` (`name_first`), called at the end of the upright arm in `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs`.\n- The MCP kind name `flute_short`: `crates/app/src/mcp/job.rs`. The located move: `crates/app/src/warned_moves.rs`. The folded UI line: `crates/ui/src/operations.rs`.\n- The decision: `docs/decisions/3525-flute-reach-law.md`.\n\nWhy a warning only beside a body finding: the first form blocked the post for a wider shank. `tool_body_beside_shank::t31_verify_judges_shank_at_6_35_below_38_1_and_catches_real_holder_hit` disproved it: that 2D Contour cuts 25 mm with a 14.478 mm flute and verifies clean. `t31` asserts that the clean program has no finding at all, so a clean path gets the note alone. The text claims no contact and does not say that the shank is wider: the `ToolGeom` of `t31` reads a 17.5 mm shank radius (widened to its holder profile) over a 6.35 mm shank.\n\n## Readings\n\n- #3319 case (`fig8.step`, `EM-0800-4FL` with flute 10, Top = stock top, Bottom = selection +1.5, stepdown 10): `flute_short` first, depth 20.500 mm; then the `shank_hit` findings and the three `RapidInStock` findings of #3319; the post is refused on the shank findings.\n- The same job with the catalog flute (20 mm): the same, depth 20.500 mm.\n- Flute 25 mm: no note, no warning.\n- Shank diameter = cutter diameter, flute 10 mm: the note first, no warning, and the program posts.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/sim/tests/flute_reach.rs` (new, 3 tests): `a_cut_past_the_flute_is_named_at_the_first_deep_move` (exact warning and note texts, first deep move, advisory), `a_flute_longer_than_the_cut_gives_no_finding`, `rapids_and_unstated_flutes_are_not_read`.\n- `crates/app/tests/flute_reach.rs` (new, 4 tests):\n  - `a_ten_mm_flute_names_its_cause_before_the_rapid_findings`: the #3319 case. It is `#[ignore]` heavy lane, because it takes about 65 s in debug. It passes in release.\n  - `the_catalog_flute_names_its_cause_before_the_shank_findings`: a plain debug test of the same job with the 20 mm catalog flute, about 35 s. It is not a light twin: it runs in the debug suite.\n  - `a_twenty_five_mm_flute_gets_no_flute_finding`.\n  - `a_same_diameter_shank_past_the_flute_is_an_advisory_note`.\n\n## Changed asserts\n\n- `mcp_verify::verify_is_not_ok_while_an_ops_own_warnings_hold_the_post`:\n  - old: every finding is `shank_hit` and holds the post;\n  - new: `findings[0]` is `flute_short` with `blocks_post` false, there is more than one finding, and every finding after it is `shank_hit` and holds the post. The asserts that `ok` is false, that `held_by` is `[\"C1\"]`, and that the post is refused stay.\n- `strategy_fallback::an_adaptive_fallback_to_offset_rings_is_a_warning`: no change. That path has no body finding, so it gets the note only, and \"no other warning\" holds.\n- `shoulder_adaptive::containment_outside_without_stock_clears_with_extension_never_the_recess`: no change. Same reason: `warns == 1` holds, and the note asserts use `any`.\n- `tool_body_beside_shank::t31_verify_judges_shank_at_6_35_below_38_1_and_catches_real_holder_hit`: no change, green.\n\nNo assert is removed.\n\n## Gate (head 274ca1483)\n\n- Quick plan (`--base` the merge base): 390 steps. The selected subset ran: 103 steps green, 0 failed, 0 stalled, 2616 tests passed, 26 ignored. The subset is:\n  - all `sim suites` steps;\n  - the touched `motion` steps;\n  - `ui suites: lib` (1477 passed) and `ui suites: operations`;\n  - the app steps `lib`, `verify*`, `strategy_fallback`, `offset_pass_start`, `posting`, `solid_law_goldens`, `first_part_programs`, the three `example_catalog*` suites, `flute_reach`, `mcp_verify`, and each app step whose name has shank, holder, collision, rapid, warning, warned, pocket, offset, adaptive, contour or clearance.\n- `gate batch --only`: `app suites: golden_cl`, `app suites: conformance`: green.\n- `flute_reach` (app) in release with `--include-ignored`: 4 passed.\n- clippy `-D warnings`: `-p camcraft-sim --all-targets`, `-p camcraft-app --lib --tests`, `-p camcraft-ui --all-targets`: clean.\n- Light lane: not run. The dry-run lists two motion twins (`the_slot_keeps_its_verdict_under_sub_micron_perturbations_light`, `wide_rectangular_pocket_is_cleared_by_parallel_lanes_light`). The motion release build is cold, and this diff does not touch motion.\n\nWhat moved: no golden, no catalog program, no posted output. The pinned warning list of `mcp_verify` moved (above).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The 287 quick-plan steps outside the subset (mostly turning, wire, probe and multi-axis suites). Their kinds are not judged by the law.\n- A stock with steps: the depth is read against the stock top, so a stepped stock can give a depth that is too large at one place.\n- The UI fold line, seen in a window (no window was started).\n- No heavy lane: P3.\n\nChangelog: A 2D Pocket, Adaptive, Offset or Contour that cuts deeper than its tool's flute length now says so first: a note with the tool, the flute length and the depth, and an advisory `flute_short` warning before the shank or holder findings that it explains.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\nRefs #3319\nRefs #3520\nFixes #3525\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
